thers to  tell you what the characters looked like  you can take down some of these  dictionaries of biography and read every  incredible in a conceivable detail and  they had to ever tells you how tall they  were what color their eyes were and and  what they look like or what their  weaknesses or or physical handicaps may  have been which may be the as important  as anything one can know about them well  among the other points that mrs. lively  makes about history is in again her  wonderful novel moon tiger in which  Claudia Hampton says I she is the  historian I have the last the last word  that's the historians privilege and so  it's my last word privilege to say the  Penelope Lively is pure gold and if  there's anything more exciting more  uplifting more intellectually  stimulating than read reading Penelope  lively for the first time it's reading  her  second time
 

